    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0689" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12644.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-27T16:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1914, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Replying to your July 25, 5 p.m. Governor Carranza, in reply to Department’s
                    suggestions, will issue today a statement which he considers will be calculated
                    to allay anxiety and inspire public confidence in the City of Mexico and
                    elsewhere. In regard to personal guaranties, all concerned should remember that
                    the demand of the Constitutionalists is for unconditional surrender. This will
                    be vigorously insisted upon. Those entitled to protection will not be molested;
                    others will be dealt with as circumstances of each case demand. Property rights
                    will be respected and the property and rights of foreigners will be accorded the
                    most ample guaranties. It is possible that Spaniards may expect trouble, as
                    elsewhere. Excess of any kind will not be permitted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
